IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `sg-core`
IMPORT `sga1-rights`

-- Tests for sga1-rights.l4 (ss 64 to 68). Every expected value is written from the text of the section, beside the assertion.
-- Arguments are positional, in the order of each function's GIVEN.

§ `Section 64: rights and powers attaching shares`

-- (1) Arguments: the thing is a share in a company; section 21, section 76J or a written law to the contrary provides otherwise; the constitution negates the right; subsection (4) protects the right.
#ASSERT `s 64(1) the share confers on the holder the right to one vote on a poll on the resolution` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- the constitution has negated the right, as subsection (3) lets it
#ASSERT `s 64(1) the share confers on the holder the right to one vote on a poll on the resolution` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- but not where subsection (4) protects it
#ASSERT `s 64(1) the share confers on the holder the right to one vote on a poll on the resolution` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- the text defers to sections 21 and 76J and to a written law to the contrary: not answered here
#ASSERT `s 64(1) the share confers on the holder the right to one vote on a poll on the resolution` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 64(1) the share confers on the holder the right to one vote on a poll on the resolution` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- not a share in a company
#ASSERT `s 64(1) the share confers on the holder the right to one vote on a poll on the resolution` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- (2) Arguments: the constitution so provides; all calls or other sums personally payable have been paid.
#ASSERT `s 64(2) the member is not entitled to vote by reason of the constitution's provision` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 64(2) the member is not entitled to vote by reason of the constitution's provision` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- a constitution without the provision: the subsection says nothing
#ASSERT `s 64(2) the member is not entitled to vote by reason of the constitution's provision` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 64(2) the member is not entitled to vote by reason of the constitution's provision` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

-- (3) Arguments: the constitution negates or alters the right; the constitution adds to the right; subsection (4) protects the right; section 64A prevents it.
#ASSERT `s 64(3) the constitution may negate, alter or add to the right` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 64(3) the constitution may negate, alter or add to the right` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- "Subject to subsection (4)": the protected right cannot be negated or altered
#ASSERT `s 64(3) the constitution may negate, alter or add to the right` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- adding to a protected right is not negating or altering it
#ASSERT `s 64(3) the constitution may negate, alter or add to the right` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- "Subject to ... section 64A": delegated
#ASSERT `s 64(3) the constitution may negate, alter or add to the right` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- the constitution has done nothing
#ASSERT `s 64(3) the constitution may negate, alter or add to the right` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- (4) Arguments: the share is a specified share; the resolution is a voluntary winding-up resolution under section 160 of the IRDA 2018; the resolution is to vary a right attached to a specified share and conferred on the holder.
#ASSERT `s 64(4) the right of the holder of the specified share to at least one vote on a poll on the resolution may be negated or altered` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 64(4) the right of the holder of the specified share to at least one vote on a poll on the resolution may be negated or altered` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- another resolution, or a share that is not a specified share
#ASSERT `s 64(4) the right of the holder of the specified share to at least one vote on a poll on the resolution may be negated or altered` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 64(4) the right of the holder of the specified share to at least one vote on a poll on the resolution may be negated or altered` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- (5) Arguments: a share in the company, by whatever name called; but for subsection (4) it does not entitle the holder to vote at a general meeting.
#ASSERT `s 64(5) "specified share" the share is a specified share` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 64(5) "specified share" the share is a specified share` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 64(5) "specified share" the share is a specified share` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- (6) Argument: the right is a right of a person under section 74.
#ASSERT `s 64(6) section 64 limits or derogates from the right` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 64(6) section 64 limits or derogates from the right` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Section 64A: issue of shares with different voting rights by a public company`

-- (1) Arguments: public company; the issue of the classes is provided for in the constitution; the constitution sets out the rights attached to each class.
#ASSERT `s 64A(1) different classes of shares in the public company may be issued` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- "only if": either condition missing gives the text's own "no"
#ASSERT `s 64A(1) different classes of shares in the public company may be issued` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 64A(1) different classes of shares in the public company may be issued` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 64A(1) different classes of shares in the public company may be issued` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- a private company is not covered by the subsection
#ASSERT `s 64A(1) different classes of shares in the public company may be issued` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

-- (2) Arguments: public company; the conditions of subsection (1)(a) and (b) are met; the shares confer special, limited or conditional voting rights, or none.
#ASSERT `s 64A(2) the shares in the public company may confer special, limited or conditional voting rights, or no voting rights` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 64A(2) the shares in the public company may confer special, limited or conditional voting rights, or no voting rights` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 64A(2) the shares in the public company may confer special, limited or conditional voting rights, or no voting rights` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 64A(2) the shares in the public company may confer special, limited or conditional voting rights, or no voting rights` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- (3) Arguments: public company; the issuance confers special, limited or conditional voting rights, or none; approved by the members by special resolution.
#ASSERT `s 64A(3) the public company is barred from the issuance` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 64A(3) the public company is barred from the issuance` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- an issuance conferring ordinary voting rights, or a private company: not covered
#ASSERT `s 64A(3) the public company is barred from the issuance` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 64A(3) the public company is barred from the issuance` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- EXPECT BREACH
#TRACE `s 64A(3) a public company must not issue shares with special, limited, conditional or no voting rights without approval by special resolution` "Acme Public Ltd" AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Company "Acme Public Ltd" DOES `s 64A(3) undertake an issuance of shares that confers special, limited or conditional voting rights, or no voting rights, without approval by special resolution` AT 1

-- EXPECT RESIDUAL
#TRACE `s 64A(3) a public company must not issue shares with special, limited, conditional or no voting rights without approval by special resolution` "Acme Public Ltd" AT 0 WITH

-- (4) Arguments: public company; it has one or more classes with special, limited, conditional or no voting rights; the notice specifies the rights of each such class.
#ASSERT `s 64A(4) the notice of the general meeting falls short of what the subsection requires` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 64A(4) the notice of the general meeting falls short of what the subsection requires` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- the "Where" gate: no such class, or a private company: the duty does not arise
#ASSERT `s 64A(4) the notice of the general meeting falls short of what the subsection requires` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 64A(4) the notice of the general meeting falls short of what the subsection requires` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- (5) Argument: the right is a right of a person under section 74.
#ASSERT `s 64A(5) section 64A limits or derogates from the right` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 64A(5) section 64A limits or derogates from the right` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- (6) Arguments: private company; the constitution forbids the issue of shares of different classes.
#ASSERT `s 64A(6) the private company may issue shares of different classes, including shares with special, limited or conditional voting rights or no voting rights` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- "subject to its constitution"
#ASSERT `s 64A(6) the private company may issue shares of different classes, including shares with special, limited or conditional voting rights or no voting rights` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- a public company is not covered by the private company's right
#ASSERT `s 64A(6) the private company may issue shares of different classes, including shares with special, limited or conditional voting rights or no voting rights` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Section 65: differences in calls and payments, and reserve liability`

-- (1) Arguments: the constitution authorises the company to exercise the power; the power.
#ASSERT `s 65(1) the company may exercise the power` TRUE `s 65(1)(a) make arrangements on the issue of shares for varying the amounts and times of payment of calls as between shareholders` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 65(1) the company may exercise the power` TRUE `s 65(1)(b) accept from a member the whole or a part of the amount remaining unpaid on any shares although no part of that amount has been called up` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 65(1) the company may exercise the power` TRUE (`s 65(1)(c) pay dividends in proportion to the amount paid up on each share` TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- (c) is given "where a larger amount is paid up on some shares than on others"
#ASSERT `s 65(1) the company may exercise the power` TRUE (`s 65(1)(c) pay dividends in proportion to the amount paid up on each share` FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
-- not authorised by the constitution: the "if" gate is unmet; the text does not say the company may not
#ASSERT `s 65(1) the company may exercise the power` FALSE `s 65(1)(a) make arrangements on the issue of shares for varying the amounts and times of payment of calls as between shareholders` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 65(1) the company may exercise the power` TRUE `s 65(1) some other power` EQUALS NOTHING

-- (2) Arguments: limited company; the special resolution has been passed.
#ASSERT `s 65(2) the limited company may determine that a portion of its uncalled share capital is not capable of being called up except in a winding up` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 65(2) the limited company may determine that a portion of its uncalled share capital is not capable of being called up except in a winding up` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 65(2) the limited company may determine that a portion of its uncalled share capital is not capable of being called up except in a winding up` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- the effect: the passed resolution; the portion had not been called up
#ASSERT `s 65(2) the portion is capable of being called up other than in the event and for the purposes of the company being wound up` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 65(2) the portion is capable of being called up other than in the event and for the purposes of the company being wound up` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 65(2) the portion is capable of being called up other than in the event and for the purposes of the company being wound up` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- the saving: rights acquired before the passing of the resolution
#ASSERT `s 65(2) the resolution affects the rights of the person` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 65(2) the resolution affects the rights of the person` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Section 66: share warrants`

-- (1) Arguments: the warrant states that the bearer is entitled to the shares specified; it enables the shares to be transferred by delivery.
#ASSERT `s 66(1) the company is barred from issuing the share warrant` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 66(1) the company is barred from issuing the share warrant` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 66(1) the company is barred from issuing the share warrant` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

-- EXPECT BREACH
#TRACE `s 66(1) a company must not issue a share warrant to bearer` "Acme Public Ltd" AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Company "Acme Public Ltd" DOES `s 66(1) issue a share warrant stating that the bearer is entitled to the shares specified and enabling them to be transferred by delivery of the warrant` AT 1

-- EXPECT RESIDUAL
#TRACE `s 66(1) a company must not issue a share warrant to bearer` "Acme Public Ltd" AT 0 WITH

-- (2) Arguments: the day the share warrant was issued; the day on which the question is asked.
-- the 2-year period after 1 July 2015 opens on 2 July 2015 and ends on 1 July 2017
#ASSERT `s 66(2) the bearer is entitled to surrender the share warrant for cancellation and to have the bearer's name entered in the register of members` (Date 1 1 1960) (Date 2 7 2015) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 66(2) the bearer is entitled to surrender the share warrant for cancellation and to have the bearer's name entered in the register of members` (Date 1 1 1960) (Date 1 7 2017) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 66(2) the bearer is entitled to surrender the share warrant for cancellation and to have the bearer's name entered in the register of members` (Date 1 1 1960) (Date 2 7 2017) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 66(2) the bearer is entitled to surrender the share warrant for cancellation and to have the bearer's name entered in the register of members` (Date 1 1 1960) (Date 1 7 2015) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 66(2) the bearer is entitled to surrender the share warrant for cancellation and to have the bearer's name entered in the register of members` (Date 1 1 1960) (Date 1 1 2015) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- "issued before 29 December 1967": the day before is covered, the day itself and later days are not
#ASSERT `s 66(2) the bearer is entitled to surrender the share warrant for cancellation and to have the bearer's name entered in the register of members` (Date 28 12 1967) (Date 1 1 2016) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 66(2) the bearer is entitled to surrender the share warrant for cancellation and to have the bearer's name entered in the register of members` (Date 29 12 1967) (Date 1 1 2016) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 66(2) the bearer is entitled to surrender the share warrant for cancellation and to have the bearer's name entered in the register of members` (Date 1 1 1980) (Date 1 1 2016) EQUALS NOTHING

-- (3) Arguments: the warrant was issued before 29 December 1967; the company entered the bearer's name in the register; the warrant was surrendered and cancelled; the person incurred loss by reason of the entry.
#ASSERT `s 66(3) the company is responsible for the loss incurred by the person` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 66(3) the company is responsible for the loss incurred by the person` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 66(3) the company is responsible for the loss incurred by the person` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 66(3) the company is responsible for the loss incurred by the person` FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 66(3) the company is responsible for the loss incurred by the person` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- (4) Arguments: the day the share warrant was issued; accounted for by the expiry of the 2-year period; the day on which the question is asked.
-- the period expires with 1 July 2017: from 2 July 2017 the unaccounted-for warrant is one the company must cancel
#ASSERT `s 66(4) the share warrant is one the company must cancel` (Date 1 1 1960) FALSE (Date 2 7 2017) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 66(4) the share warrant is one the company must cancel` (Date 1 1 1960) FALSE (Date 1 7 2017) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 66(4) the share warrant is one the company must cancel` (Date 1 1 1960) TRUE (Date 2 7 2017) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 66(4) the share warrant is one the company must cancel` (Date 1 1 1980) FALSE (Date 2 7 2017) EQUALS NOTHING
-- the company is not responsible for the loss by reason of such cancellation
#ASSERT `s 66(4) the company is responsible for the loss incurred by the person by reason of the cancellation` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 66(4) the company is responsible for the loss incurred by the person by reason of the cancellation` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- The duty to cancel has no deadline in the text, so it cannot be breached: a late act still reads FULFILLED, and no act reads RESIDUAL.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 66(4) a company must cancel a share warrant issued before 29 December 1967 that is unaccounted for by the expiry of the 2-year period` "Acme Public Ltd" 7 AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Company "Acme Public Ltd" DOES `s 66(4) cancel a share warrant issued before 29 December 1967 that is unaccounted for by the expiry of the 2-year period` AT 5

-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 66(4) a company must cancel a share warrant issued before 29 December 1967 that is unaccounted for by the expiry of the 2-year period` "Acme Public Ltd" 7 AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Company "Acme Public Ltd" DOES `s 66(4) cancel a share warrant issued before 29 December 1967 that is unaccounted for by the expiry of the 2-year period` AT 5000

-- EXPECT RESIDUAL
#TRACE `s 66(4) a company must cancel a share warrant issued before 29 December 1967 that is unaccounted for by the expiry of the 2-year period` "Acme Public Ltd" 7 AT 0 WITH

§ `Section 67: use of share capital to pay the expenses of issuing new shares`

-- (1) Argument: the expenses (including brokerage or commission) were incurred directly in the issue of new shares.
#ASSERT `s 67(1) the company may use its share capital to pay the expenses` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 67(1) the company may use its share capital to pay the expenses` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- (2) Argument: the payment is made under subsection (1).
#ASSERT `s 67(2) the payment is to be taken as reducing the amount of share capital of the company` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 67(2) the payment is to be taken as reducing the amount of share capital of the company` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Section 68: issue of shares for no consideration`

-- Arguments: the company has a share capital; no consideration is payable to the issuing company for the shares.
#ASSERT `s 68 the company may issue the shares for no consideration` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 68 the company may issue the shares for no consideration` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 68 the company may issue the shares for no consideration` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
